 "response": {
  "text": "Yes — for Indian skin tones, I’d prioritize a **SPF 50+ / PA++++ sunscreen with modern chemical or tinted filters**, rather than a traditional mineral sunscreen, because it’s much less likely to look grey/ashy. [www.drsheths.com](https://www.drsheths.com/blogs/skin-care/sunscreens-that-dont-leave-a-white-cast-for-indian-skin?utm_source=chatgpt.com)\n\n### 🥇 My best overall pick: Re'equil Ultra Matte Dry Touch SPF 50\n\n### [Re'equil Sunscreen SPF 50 PA++++ Ultra Matte Dry Touch Gel]()\n*₹310.50*\n\n**Why I’d pick it:**  \n- Very good choice for **Indian heat and humidity**\n- Matte, non-greasy finish\n- Generally blends without an obvious white cast\n- Particularly good for **oily/combination skin** [www.nykaa.com](https://www.nykaa.com/beauty-blog/ultimate-guide-choosing-sunscreen-for-indian-skin?utm_source=chatgpt.com)\n\n### Other good choices\n\n### [Minimalist Light Fluid Face Sunscreen SPF 50]()\n*₹315*\n\n### [Dot & Key Watermelon Cooling Sunscreen SPF 50+ PA++++]()\n*₹400*\n\n### [The Derma Co 1% Hyaluronic Tinted Sunscreen Gel]()\n*₹496*\n\n### [Fixderma Shadow Tinted Sunscreen]()\n*₹297*\n\n- **Minimalist Light Fluid SPF 50** — best if you want a very lightweight, fluid texture.\n- **Dot & Key Watermelon SPF 50+** — better if you prefer a hydrating, dewy feel; the brand specifically describes it as zero-white-cast. [www.dotandkey.com](https://www.dotandkey.com/collections/sunscreen?utm_source=chatgpt.com)\n- **The Derma Co tinted sunscreen** — great if you're particularly worried about any visible cast because the tint helps it blend into skin.\n- **Fixderma Shadow Tinted** — another good tinted option.\n\n**If you tell me your skin type (oily/dry/combination) and roughly your skin tone (fair/medium/wheatish/deep), I can narrow it down to the single best one for you.**",
